{"id": "EUVD-2026-67036", "enisaUuid": "b0d39ff3-26a8-33a4-8649-ca43fe73bc68", "description": "openssl_encrypt versions before 1.4.9 fail to authenticate recovery-slot presence in envelope-format encrypted files, allowing attackers to remove recovery slots without re-encrypting the payload. Attackers can modify the file header to delete recovery-slot fields and bypass authentication, silently removing recovery paths the owner deliberately added.", "datePublished": "2026-08-27T14:50:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T15:21:16", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/jahlives/openssl_encrypt/security/advisories/GHSA-grhj-cpmg-f5mx", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openssl-encrypt-before-1.4.9-authentication-bypass-via-recovery-slot-removal"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-81680", "GHSA-59ww-7vhf-hj2q", "PYSEC-2026-3957"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "da53485b-b307-3bbf-b969-0adc9889e29e", "product": {"name": "openssl_encrypt", "vendor": {"name": "jahlives"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.4.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2c3848d6-25e9-385b-b98d-665d659b6fbb", "vendor": {"name": "jahlives"}}], "isExploited": false}